# paper1-closed-form.meta.ttl — claim annotations for paper1-closed-form.md
#
# Each published statistic in the article carries an invisible anchor at the
# number, <!--@c-<id>-->, and is described here as a schema:Claim keyed to that
# id. The metadata lives OUT of the prose for four reasons:
#
#   1. it is a first-class .ttl, so it inherits the repo's existing rule that
#      every Turtle file is validated with rdflib after editing;
#   2. it composes directly with claims.ttl and data-graph.ttl — the three can
#      be loaded into one graph and queried together;
#   3. human drafters editing prose cannot corrupt it. Inline blocks lived in
#      HTML comments, where a reflowed paragraph or a stray double hyphen closes
#      the comment early and silently eats the annotation;
#   4. it survives a format change. The human draft may not stay markdown; an
#      inline HTML comment does not follow it to LaTeX or a word processor, a
#      sidecar keyed by id does. If the anchors are lost in such a move, the
#      claims are still fully described here and can be re-anchored — which is
#      why every claim carries schema:text.
#
# RETIRED 2026-07-31, with the frozen protocol (P_a,g). The claims below left
# the paper when sections 3.1, 2.3.3, 3.4.3 and 4.3.1-4.3.3 were removed:
#   pool.regime.f3d and pool.regime.sim went with section 3.3 (per-ride physics
#   results) when it was dropped as duplicating 2.2's method statement.
#   d1.blind.f3.med, d1.f1.uncorrected.med, d1.f2.split.med, d1.parity.signtest,
#   d2.f3.med, d2.tost.worse, e46.ag.switched.med, e46.eps_applied.sub3
# plus pool34.sim.med, pool35.f3d.med and d6.f3f.collapse earlier. They are not
# withdrawn as findings -- each remains in the lab journal with its entry -- but
# they are no longer ARTICLE claims, because the protocol that produced them is
# no longer a protocol the paper runs. Entry 50 is the reason: eps carries ~7% of
# the error variance, so a frozen-constant result measured how wrong the assumed
# constants were rather than how good the law is.
#
# Validate: python3 -c "import rdflib; rdflib.Graph().parse('research/article/paper1-closed-form.meta.ttl')"
# Checked by research/scripts/check_paper_stats.py

@prefix schema:  <http://schema.org/> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix cito:    <http://purl.org/spar/cito/> .
@prefix prov:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix pc:      <https://danlessa.github.io/bicycling-energy-model/paper-claims#> .
@prefix dg:      <https://danlessa.github.io/bicycling-energy-model/data-graph#> .
@prefix claims:  <https://danlessa.github.io/bicycling-energy-model/claims#> .






















<#c-e50.eps.share> a schema:Claim ;
  schema:text "eps accounts for 0.070 of F3 prediction-error variance (total-order Sobol index), against 0.553 for CdA" ;
  dcterms:type "derived" ;
  pc:value 0.070 ;
  pc:gateSection "3p" ;
  cito:citesAsEvidence dg:o_e50 ;
  pc:preRegistered true ;
  rdfs:comment "The measurement that moved the deficit theory out of paper 1 and into section 4.4.2 as future work" .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Entry 52 — the A-chain. One protocol (P_f,r), one random split of D3-D6,
# forms selected by cross-validation on the training half and scored once on
# the held-out 305. These replace the frozen-grid claims retired above, whose
# prose went with section 3.3's rewrite: that section reported a protocol the
# paper no longer runs, and Entry 50 showed why -- eps is ~7% of the error
# variance, so a frozen-constant table measured how wrong the assumed constants
# were rather than how good the law is.

<#c-e52.f3.med> a schema:Claim ;
  schema:text "F3 median |D%| 3.24 [2.75, 3.50] on the held-out half of D3-D6, n = 305" ;
  dcterms:type "out-of-sample" ;
  pc:value 3.24 ;
  pc:gateSection "3q" ;
  cito:citesAsEvidence dg:o_ppaz, dg:o_jaam, dg:o_danlessa, dg:o_skc ;
  prov:wasDerivedFrom claims:assert12 ;
  rdfs:comment "THE headline. Rides used neither to fit eps nor to choose the form. Held out in eps and form, NOT in the per-ride constants -- the inversion is data preparation and runs before the split -- and re-scored as that inversion was revised (Entries 52/55/57; paper section 3.1.4). Value after the Entry 57 rider-median fallbacks; 3.39 before them" .

<#c-e52.f3.bias> a schema:Claim ;
  schema:text "F3 median signed D% +0.07 [-0.31, 0.70] on the held-out half of D3-D6" ;
  dcterms:type "out-of-sample" ;
  pc:value 0.07 ;
  pc:gateSection "3q" ;
  cito:citesAsEvidence dg:o_ppaz, dg:o_jaam, dg:o_danlessa, dg:o_skc ;
  prov:wasDerivedFrom claims:assert12 ;
  rdfs:comment "Paired with the accuracy figure per the house rule: accuracy alone hides bias cancellation" .

<#c-e52.fbase.med> a schema:Claim ;
  schema:text "F_base median |D%| 3.19 [2.73, 3.74] on the same held-out half, as a comparator outside selection" ;
  dcterms:type "out-of-sample" ;
  pc:value 3.19 ;
  pc:gateSection "3q" ;
  cito:citesAsEvidence dg:o_ppaz, dg:o_jaam, dg:o_danlessa, dg:o_skc ;
  prov:wasDerivedFrom claims:assert12 ;
  rdfs:comment "The comparator, outside selection. Parity with F3, not superiority either way: the paired sign test is a coin flip. The earlier gap (Entry 52) traced to a drag area inferred at one speed and used at another, and closed with eq. (5) (Entry 55)" .

<#c-e52.eps> a schema:Claim ;
  schema:text "the descent constant refits to eps = 0.294 on the training half, against 0.282 on the test half's own optimum (tau held at 6 m)" ;
  dcterms:type "out-of-sample" ;
  pc:value 0.294 ;
  pc:gateSection "3q" ;
  cito:citesAsEvidence dg:o_ppaz, dg:o_jaam, dg:o_danlessa, dg:o_skc ;
  prov:wasDerivedFrom claims:assert12 ;
  rdfs:comment "The two-way agreement is the identifiability check: the constant is a property of the data, not of which rides were drawn" .

<#c-e52.twin> a schema:Claim ;
  schema:text "82% of held-out rides have a same-rider training ride within 5% on distance and 10% on ascent" ;
  dcterms:type "out-of-sample" ;
  pc:value 82 ;
  pc:gateSection "3q" ;
  cito:citesAsEvidence dg:o_ppaz, dg:o_jaam, dg:o_danlessa, dg:o_skc ;
  prov:wasDerivedFrom claims:assert12 ;
  rdfs:comment "The exposure a random split carries, measured rather than assumed away. 3.24 is a repeat-route error" .

<#c-e52.f3.med.abs> a schema:Claim ;
  schema:text "F3 median |D%| 3.24 [2.75, 3.50] on the held-out half of D3-D6, n = 305 (abstract restatement)" ;
  dcterms:type "out-of-sample" ;
  pc:value 3.24 ;
  pc:gateSection "3q" ;
  cito:citesAsEvidence dg:o_ppaz, dg:o_jaam, dg:o_danlessa, dg:o_skc ;
  prov:wasDerivedFrom claims:assert12 ;
  rdfs:comment "Same statistic as c-e52.f3.med, anchored separately because the abstract prints it independently of section 3.3 and a human drafter may rewrite either without the other" .

<#c-e52.f4.med> a schema:Claim ;
  schema:text "F4 median |D%| 2.86 [2.58, 3.39] on the held-out half of D3-D6, n = 305" ;
  dcterms:type "out-of-sample" ;
  pc:value 2.86 ;
  pc:gateSection "3q" ;
  cito:citesAsEvidence dg:o_ppaz, dg:o_jaam, dg:o_danlessa, dg:o_skc ;
  prov:wasDerivedFrom claims:assert12 ;
  rdfs:comment "The TOTALS-ONLY form, and the one the recipe is built on. Reported beside F3 because the two need different inputs, not because one is better -- their intervals overlap and both biases contain zero" .

<#c-e52.parity.signtest> a schema:Claim ;
  schema:text "against F_base on the held-out half, the selected form is closer on 153 of 305 rides: paired sign test p = 1.00" ;
  dcterms:type "out-of-sample" ;
  pc:value 153 ;
  pc:gateSection "3q" ;
  cito:citesAsEvidence dg:o_e52_summary ;
  rdfs:comment "The parity claim, and an absence of evidence rather than an equivalence result (the registered TOST has not been run on this split). Lab journal Entry 57 recorded 152 of 305; the 2026-09-25 re-run of the same chain printed 153, p = 1.00 either way. Gated since 2026-11-07: e52_split.py writes sign_win / sign_los / sign_p to e52_summary.csv and section 3q holds the count exactly and p to the printed digits. Was 149 of 305, p = 0.73 before Entry 57" .

<#c-e52.parity.signtest.abs> a schema:Claim ;
  schema:text "against F_base on the held-out half, the selected form is closer on 153 of 305 rides, p = 1.00 (abstract restatement)" ;
  dcterms:type "out-of-sample" ;
  pc:value 153 ;
  pc:gateSection "3q" ;
  cito:citesAsEvidence dg:o_e52_summary ;
  rdfs:comment "Same statistic as c-e52.parity.signtest, anchored separately for the reason c-e52.f3.med.abs is: the abstract prints the central claim independently of section 3.1.3" .

<#c-e52.eps.test> a schema:Claim ;
  schema:text "the held-out half's own eps optimum is 0.282 at the selected tau of 6 m, against 0.294 fitted on the training half" ;
  dcterms:type "in-sample" ;
  pc:value 0.282 ;
  pc:gateSection "3q" ;
  cito:citesAsEvidence dg:o_e52_summary ;
  rdfs:comment "The other half of c-e52.eps's identifiability check, and in-sample by construction: fitted ON the held-out half, after scoring, and never fed back into selection. The paper printed 0.255 -- Entry 52's value, under the superseded segment drag estimator -- until 2026-09-25. Gated since 2026-11-07: e52_split.py writes eps_test_opt to e52_summary.csv" .

<#c-e54.transfer> a schema:Claim ;
  schema:text "fitting eps on one rider and scoring it on the other riders' held-out rides costs 0.05 pp of median |D%|, inside the registered 1.0 pp margin (the median pools within- and cross-landscape donor-recipient pairs)" ;
  dcterms:type "out-of-sample" ;
  pc:value 0.05 ;
  pc:gateSection "3r" ;
  cito:citesAsEvidence dg:o_ppaz, dg:o_jaam, dg:o_danlessa, dg:o_skc ;
  prov:wasDerivedFrom claims:assert12 ;
  rdfs:comment "The paper's one hypothesis (section 1.3). Strict transfer: a different person AND rides already held out from selection. The all-pairs median mixes within- and cross-region transfers (Entry 60); the within-region-only LORO check is registered as untested" .

<#c-e60.br> a schema:Claim ;
  schema:text "regional eps on D3-D5 gives 2.85 [2.23, 3.55] held-out, against 3.67 for the single pool" ;
  dcterms:type "out-of-sample" ; pc:value 2.85 ; pc:gateSection "3t" ;
  cito:citesAsEvidence dg:o_ppaz, dg:o_jaam, dg:o_danlessa ;
  prov:wasDerivedFrom claims:assert12 ;
  rdfs:comment "Entry 60. The signed pair matters more than the accuracy: one pool biases the two regions in opposite directions (-1.31 vs +1.95), which cancels in any pooled average" .

<#c-e60.eu> a schema:Claim ;
  schema:text "regional eps on D6 gives 1.73 [1.27, 2.30] held-out, against 2.65 for the single pool" ;
  dcterms:type "out-of-sample" ; pc:value 1.73 ; pc:gateSection "3t" ;
  cito:citesAsEvidence dg:o_skc ;
  prov:wasDerivedFrom claims:assert12 ;
  rdfs:comment "Entry 60. Decisive on the paired test (74/109, p = 0.0002) where the Sao Paulo half is the same size but not individually significant" .
